Add the kbase backend to libpankmod_lib.

Adds pan_kmod_kbase.c to the pan_kmod library and points it at the kbase
UAPI headers, which are not part of Mesa - they're vendored in the
PanVK2KBase repo (third_party/kbase-uapi-<version>/).

Three things the backend needs beyond the source file itself:

  -DMALI_USE_CSF=1   Selects the CSF (Valhall v10+) ioctl surface, matching
                     every other consumer of these headers in PanVK2KBase.

  -include kconfig_shim.h
                     Resolves IS_ENABLED() for MTK-derived header sets
                     (r49p1 uses it around vendor debug fields) outside a
                     kernel build tree. Harmless for header sets that don't,
                     like r44p0.

  -I<kbase uapi dir> The vendored headers.

The two absolute paths below are placeholders - substitute your own
PanVK2KBase checkout. `make mesa-backend-sync` does this substitution for
you rather than applying this patch literally.

VERIFIED: this exact change builds. Mesa 26.3.0-devel (7296f9a), native
x86_64 Linux, meson 1.11.2 / LLVM 18.1.3.

--- a/src/panfrost/lib/kmod/meson.build
+++ b/src/panfrost/lib/kmod/meson.build
@@ -5,13 +5,16 @@ libpankmod_lib_files = files(
   'pan_kmod.c',
   'panfrost_kmod.c',
   'panthor_kmod.c',
+  'pan_kmod_kbase.c',
 )

 libpankmod_lib = static_library(
   'pankmod_lib',
   [libpankmod_lib_files],
   include_directories : [inc_include, inc_src, inc_panfrost],
-  c_args : [no_override_init_args],
+  c_args : [no_override_init_args, '-DMALI_USE_CSF=1',
+            '-include', '@PANVK2KBASE@/src/utils/kconfig_shim.h',
+            '-I@PANVK2KBASE@/third_party/kbase-uapi-r49p1'],
   gnu_symbol_visibility : 'hidden',
   dependencies: [dep_libdrm, idep_mesautil, idep_pan_packers, libpanfrost_model_dep],
   build_by_default : false,
